    description: `The capstone required each student to assemble a complete Employability Portfolio demonstrating every objective of the program in evidenced artifacts: a one-page resume rewritten through two review rounds with accomplishment bullets carrying measurable results; a LinkedIn profile and personal portfolio page populated with the work produced during the four weeks; a story bank of eight STAR responses drawn from real experience and rehearsed in recorded mock interviews; and a written personal leadership philosophy revised against observed behaviour. Each artifact was cross-checked for consistency — the same claim, number and tone had to survive in every document — because inconsistency is exactly what interview panels probe. The portfolio was defended live in a five-minute career pitch followed by hostile follow-up questions, and graded on evidence quality, cross-document consistency and composure under challenge. Every artifact was versioned with dated revisions in the portfolio, so reviewers could see how feedback changed the work rather than only the final state, and each claim in the resume was traced back to a dated artifact before the pitch.`,
